              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">The Hamburg Building Code (Hamburgische Bauordnung, HBauO) is decisive. Permit-exempt works and the building notification under Section 60 HBauO apply depending on size and site — we check the classification of your Hamburg site in advance and submit review-ready building documents to the competent borough office.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">HPA procedure on port land</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">On port land the Hamburg Port Authority is competent rather than the borough office. Flood protection, terp elevation of at least +1.30 m and LSBG-compliant structural design are coordinated early with HPA and LSBG — we prepare the full application documents.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">BUKEA notification for BSL-3 and GenTG</h3>
              <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">BSL-3 in Hamburg requires a permit under BioStoffV (federal law) plus a notification to BUKEA — Hamburg’s authority for environment, climate, energy and agriculture. For genetic-engineering facilities S1/S2/S3 an additional notification under the German Genetic Engineering Act (GenTG) is required. We supply the risk assessment, safety concept and complete application documents.</p>
